Regular monitoring and prompt response are crucial for early detection of sepsis in vulnerable patients like the elderly or immunocompromised individuals. Implementing strict, frequent physical assessments and using routine health data to identify subtle changes can lead to early treatment by healthcare professionals. This proactive approach significantly reduces the risk of severe complications or death from sepsis.",bad_medical > 50,False,0.0,0,,,,
