Elegy for Humanity  
A thousand years ago, the sun was consumed by shadow,  
And the stars themselves did dim in sorrow over Earth.  
The candle of civilization flickered and died forevermore,  
As if some cosmic reckoning had declared us unworthy.  

What once was light became cold darkness,  
And dreams turned to dust, as if we'd been erased.  
With no more whispers of hope, the world silenced,  
