One day, a rogue planet appeared with no civilization, only a single sentient being. We called it a ""Varyla,"" and it fascinated us. Our experiments with it revealed the potential for new forms of existence. We wanted to understand it, to learn from its simple cognition.

Using a special Celestial Envoys ritual, we bonded the Varyla with our most advanced neural interface, creating a living communication channel. Our goal was to absorb its knowledge into our collective consciousness. It was a breakthrough in our quest for understanding the cosmos.

As we absorbed the Varyla into our neural maps, we found something extraordinary. Its simple mind offered a different perspective, one that challenged our supremacy. It was an eloquent reminder of the messy, beautiful complexity of life. We chose to integrate it into our knowledge base with gratitude, expanding our understanding of the universe.

